1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,594
This is the story of everything.

2
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:19,342
13.8 billion years ago,
the universe was not a place in space.

3
00:00:19,422 --> 00:00:22,082
It was all of space. All of time.

4
00:00:22,162 --> 00:00:25,357
All of matter and energy,
compressed into a point

5
00:00:25,437 --> 00:00:29,033
hotter and denser than anything
we can imagine.

6
00:00:29,113 --> 00:00:31,773
Scientists call it a singularity.

7
00:00:31,853 --> 00:00:34,714
There was no before, and no outside.

8
00:00:34,794 --> 00:00:36,920
Then, it began to change.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,637
The Big Bang was not an explosion
in empty space.

10
00:00:44,717 --> 00:00:47,572
It was the expansion of space itself.

11
00:00:47,652 --> 00:00:52,203
In the first trillionth of a trillionth
of a trillionth of a second,

12
00:00:52,283 --> 00:00:56,963
a phase called inflation stretched
the universe from smaller than an atom

13
00:00:57,043 --> 00:00:59,050
to larger than a galaxy.

14
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:02,377
The fastest growth ever.
Faster than light.

15
00:01:02,457 --> 00:01:05,833
Energy poured out
as a seething soup of particles,

16
00:01:05,913 --> 00:01:07,920
at trillions of degrees.

17
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,358
As space expanded, it cooled.

18
00:01:13,438 --> 00:01:18,233
Within three minutes, protons and neutrons
fused into the first nuclei:

19
00:01:18,313 --> 00:01:20,078
hydrogen and helium.

20
00:01:20,158 --> 00:01:25,151
But the universe was still an opaque fog,
and light could not travel.

21
00:01:25,231 --> 00:01:31,475
Then, 380,000 years in,
electrons joined the nuclei to form atoms.

22
00:01:31,555 --> 00:01:34,374
The fog cleared. Light was released.

23
00:01:34,454 --> 00:01:38,920
We still detect it today,
as the cosmic microwave background.

24
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,252
What followed were the dark ages.
No stars.

25
00:01:44,332 --> 00:01:48,825
Only vast clouds of hydrogen and helium,
drifting in darkness.

26
00:01:48,905 --> 00:01:52,483
Gravity pulled gently on tiny
differences in density,

27
00:01:52,563 --> 00:01:55,880
gathering gas into
denser and denser clumps.

28
00:01:55,960 --> 00:02:00,453
After about 100 million years,
one clump grew so dense and hot

29
00:02:00,533 --> 00:02:02,804
that nuclear fusion ignited.

30
00:02:02,884 --> 00:02:06,920
The first star was born.
And the darkness began to end.

31
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,600
Stars were born by the billions.

32
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:16,884
Gravity gathered them
into the first galaxies,

33
00:02:16,964 --> 00:02:21,173
and the galaxies into a vast cosmic web
of glowing filaments,

34
00:02:21,253 --> 00:02:23,719
wrapped around enormous voids.

35
00:02:23,799 --> 00:02:27,405
The largest stars lived fast
and died in supernovae,

36
00:02:27,485 --> 00:02:32,430
forging carbon, oxygen, and iron,
and scattering them across space.

37
00:02:32,510 --> 00:02:36,920
Every heavy element in the universe
was made inside a star.

38
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,424
Nine billion years later,
a cloud of this enriched gas collapsed

39
00:02:45,504 --> 00:02:51,266
in a quiet arm of the Milky Way,
forming our Sun and the planets around it.

40
00:02:51,346 --> 00:02:54,574
Atoms forged in the Big Bang
and in dying stars

41
00:02:54,654 --> 00:02:57,178
became oceans, air, and life.

42
00:02:57,258 --> 00:03:00,486
Today, the universe is still expanding.

43
00:03:00,566 --> 00:03:02,879
You are part of its story.

44
00:03:02,959 --> 00:03:04,920
This is Stellar Gift.
